Description: Skip crashed browsers without a frame loader when sending them to the tab crash page.
 TabCrashHandler queues the selected browser of a crashed content process while it still has a frame loader, and
 sends it to the tab crash page once the process ended. When its window closes in between, as when Firefox quits
 while its content processes end, the browser has no frame loader left, and changing its remoteness fails a release
 assertion in nsFrameLoaderOwner::ChangeRemoteness(). With sigterm-handler-after-app-shell.patch this happens when
 SIGTERM reaches all processes of Firefox at once, as when systemd stops it: the content processes end, while Firefox
 quits cleanly and closes its windows.
Bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2094896
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344125
Applied-Upstream: 163, https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/commit/6f7b84191ac6f604eb09efe3fc4573c16a8c33e6
Last-Update: 2026-11-23
---
diff --git a/browser/modules/ContentCrashHandlers.sys.mjs b/browser/modules/ContentCrashHandlers.sys.mjs
--- a/browser/modules/ContentCrashHandlers.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/modules/ContentCrashHandlers.sys.mjs
@@ -217,7 +217,9 @@ export var TabCrashHandler = {
     let sentBrowser = false;
     for (let weakBrowser of browserQueue) {
       let browser = weakBrowser.get();
-      if (browser) {
+      // A browser whose window closed after the crash, as when Firefox quits,
+      // has no frame loader to change the remoteness of.
+      if (browser?.frameLoader) {
         if (
           this.restartRequiredBrowsers.has(browser) ||
           this.testBuildIDMismatch
